Z||000016||sqoach||01-31-2001||01:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RaeQwan:<BR><B>hey Sqoach.. wanna hear some funny   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> they made Mera's in 87   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>i think i remember reading that once. can't remember the link, tho. they started with the mera on the 87 v6 chasis. but i believe all formula's were 88.<P>brad, an easy way to tell is just check the vin #. so many fieros have been modified and put back together with different panels, it's hard to tell.<BR>88 formula: 88 coupe body w/wing, v6 engine, and "formula" written on the lower door. 87 se: notchback body with ground f/x all the way around. with a wing it would look almost exactly like an 85 gt.<P>(if any of the above information is incorrect, someone kick me)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||10
